<component><section><templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.17" extension="2015-08-01"/><code code="29762-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Social history Narrative"/><title>Social History</title><text><list><item>Singer, songwriter and guitarist; tours with his band for months at a time; performing and moving on stage are central to his work [S]</item><item>Plays football several times a week and runs most mornings [S]</item><item>Faith: Rastafari, central to how he lives and makes decisions; he asks that his clinicians understand what matters to him before he decides on any treatment [S]</item><item>Does not smoke tobacco; drinks alcohol rarely [S]</item><item>Born in Jamaica; lives with his family; supports are his family, his bandmates and his faith community. He decides who is told about his health [S]</item><item>Skin: Fitzpatrick type VI. Acral melanoma is not caused by sun exposure and is the most common type of melanoma in people with darker skin [S]</item></list></text></section></component>

